# Parent that has both its index and a child

Two files, which is the reason a case is a directory rather than a single file.
`memory/parent` has a child directory AND its own `memory.md`, so the second
rejection path must stay quiet.

This is the only input that pins the `memory.md` literal inside that path's
predicate. Swap `[ ! -f "$dir/memory.md" ]` for any name that never exists and
every reject case still fires — the predicate has simply become "has a child
directory", which condemns nine healthy rooms in this repository. Nothing that
holds one file can state it.
